# Copy to `.env` to wire the forms up to a real backend.
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle at build time and
# is therefore PUBLIC — a Formspree form ID is meant to be public (it's a
# form action URL), so that's fine; if you ever swap to something like a
# Supabase table, only ever put a publishable/anon key here, never a
# service key.
#
# Leave these unset and the forms degrade honestly: the notify form points
# visitors at the support address, and the contact form opens their mail
# client with the message pre-filled. Neither pretends to have sent anything.

# Formspree (https://formspree.io) or any endpoint accepting a JSON POST.
# Both can point at the same form ID — see the `_subject` field each form
# adds in ContactForm.jsx / NotifyForm.jsx to keep them distinguishable in
# one shared inbox.
# VITE_NOTIFY_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
